{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdio>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef vector<int> vi;\n\nconst int INF = 1000000007;\n\ninline void read(int &x) { scanf(\"%d\", &x); }\ninline void read(int &a, int &b) { scanf(\"%d %d\", &a, &b); }\ninline void read(int &a, int &b, int &c) { scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &a, &b, &c); }\ninline void read(int &a, int &b, int &c, int &d) { scanf(\"%d %d %d %d\", &a, &b, &c, &d); }\n\ninline void readln(int &x) { scanf(\"%d\\n\", &x); }\ninline void readln(int &a, int &b) { scanf(\"%d %d\\n\", &a, &b); }\ninline void readln(int &a, int &b, int &c) { scanf(\"%d %d %d\\n\", &a, &b, &c); }\ninline void readln(int &a, int &b, int &c, int &d) { scanf(\"%d %d %d %d\\n\", &a, &b, &c, &d); }\n\ninline void writeln(int x) { printf(\"%d\\n\", x); }\ninline void writeln(int a, int b) { printf(\"%d %d\\n\", a, b); }\ninline void writeln(int a, int b, int c) { printf(\"%d %d %d\\n\", a, b, c); }\ninline void writeln(int a, int b, int c, int d) { printf(\"%d %d %d %d\\n\", a, b, c, d); }\n\ninline void write(int x) { printf(\"%d\", x); }\ninline void write(int a, int b) { printf(\"%d %d\", a, b); }\ninline void write(int a, int b, int c) { printf(\"%d %d %d\", a, b, c); }\ninline void write(int a, int b, int c, int d) { printf(\"%d %d %d %d\", a, b, c, d); }\n\nvoid read_vector(vi &v, int n) {\n    int x;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        read(x);\n        v.push_back(x);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid write_vector(const vi &v) {\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < v.size(); ++i) {\n        printf(\"%d%c\", v[i], (i == v.size() - 1) ? '\\n' : ' ');\n    }\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n    int n, t;\n    vi arr;\n    read(n);\n    read_vector(arr, n);\n    sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());\n    \n    int left = 0, right = 0, max_len = 0;\n    read(t);\n    \n    while (right < n) {\n        while (right < n && arr[right] - arr[left] <= t) {\n            ++right;\n        }\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left);\n        ++left;\n    }\n    \n    writeln(max_len);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    solve();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int INF = 1000000007;\n    \n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n        \n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n        \n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n        \n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void read_vector(ArrayList<Integer> v, int n, FastReader fr) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            int x = fr.nextInt();\n            v.add(x);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void write_vector(ArrayList<Integer> v) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < v.size(); ++i) {\n            System.out.print(v.get(i));\n            if (i == v.size() - 1) {\n                System.out.println();\n            } else {\n                System.out.print(\" \");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void solve() {\n        FastReader fr = new FastReader();\n        int n = fr.nextInt();\n        ArrayList<Integer> arr = new ArrayList<>();\n        read_vector(arr, n, fr);\n        Collections.sort(arr);\n        \n        int left = 0, right = 0, max_len = 0;\n        int t = fr.nextInt();\n        \n        while (right < n) {\n            while (right < n && arr.get(right) - arr.get(left) <= t) {\n                ++right;\n            }\n            max_len = Math.max(max_len, right - left);\n            ++left;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(max_len);\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        solve();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00010179955279454589, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0009924016194418073, -2.2649508537142538e-05, -0.42870423197746277, -0.09018539637327194, -0.00010406429646536708, -1.0609570381348021e-05, -3.0040289857424796e-05, -0.00014053787162993103, -1.2159273865108844e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.4927710657939315e-05, -0.002186647616326809, -2.8013790142722428e-05, -0.5239406228065491, -0.5926209092140198, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.645074735279195e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.2811509966850281, -0.4287213087081909, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.20437870919704437, -0.6669526100158691, -0.3112730085849762, -0.6982470154762268, -3.886147169396281e-05, -4